    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Geraghty offer 6 Brownstown to the market, a substantial 5 bedroom detached residence, standing on 0.44 acre of private grounds, located in the much sought after development of Brownstown, walking distance of Ratoath village and adjacent to the GAA grounds which are located behind the residence.This spacious home has a country feel, and offers some lovely features throughout. Some of these include a large brick fireplace with solid fuel stove in the sitting room, feature beam ceiling and timber pillars throughout, a gallery landing, large laundry room/utility room and a vaulted ceiling in the sunroom, to mention but a few.There is an excellent flow to the reception rooms that link the kitchen and sunroom to the patio area and outdoor space. Two further reception rooms to the right of the entrance hall allow a recreation space for older ones and there is a large home office off this room which is perfect for hybrid working or studying.No 6 is positioned towards the entrance to this exclusive development, allowing an easy stroll to the heart of Ratoath village, where one will find trendy coffee houses, excellent restaurants, The Venue Theatre etc.For those who commute to the city or the Airport, the location provides easy access to the M2, the M3, the M50 interchange and the Park&Ride facility at Dunboyne/Clonee. There is also a regular bus services from the village.No 6 Brownstown offers a wonderful sense of privacy, on a large site, rarely found so close to a village.For transparency purposes, all bidding will be carried out on line via our unique bidding platform: \"MySherryFitz\""
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nHardwood flooring feature timber beam pillars, cast iron radiator and gallery landing\n\nGuest WC and WHB - \nWainscotting detail and window for natural light and ventilation\n\nReception Room - \nRight of hallway adjoining home office\n\nHome Office / Study Room - \nWas the original garage which was converted prior to the current owners moving in\n\nSitting Room - \nThe focal point of the sitting room is the large brick fireplace and hearth with cast iron stove insert (standalone), this room has a dual aspect, a half hexagonal window, cast iron radiators, hardwood flooring and is open plan to the dining room\n\nDining Room / Reception Room - \nFeature beam ceilings, hardwood flooring, double doors lead to the kitchen and a set of double doors also open to the garden. This room also has a brick fireplace and hearth with alcove shelving\n\nKitchen - \nStorage cupboards at base and eye level with double Belfast sink, feature beam ceilings, hardwood worktops and breakfast bar, double Neff oven, wine rack and is plumbed for dishwasher, slate tiled floor underfoot\n\nSunroom / Living Room - \nVaulted ceiling, French doors to garden and Slate flooring\n\nLaundry Room / Utility Room - \nSlate floor, plumbed for washing machine and drier, storage cupboards, sink, cloak area and exit door to garden\n\nBoiler Room - \nThe Water Filtration system is located here along with the oil-fired boiler. Separate attic area accessible from boiler room,suit conversion\n\nUpstairs - \npainted staircase with carpet to gallery landing area, access to attic spaceAiring Cupboard - large insulated tank, shelving and light installed for convenience\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, vanity basin, bath, separate shower, feature beams and window for natural light and ventilation\n\nMain Bedroom - \nVarnished floor boards, lovely high ceiling with timber beams, access to space in eaves, walk in wardrobes with two double door access points\n\nEn-Suite Shower Room - \nDual sinks with storage beneath, tiled splashback, tiled shower and large window for natural light and ventilation\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA double bedroom located at the front with access to storage in the eaves and feature timber beams\n\nBedroom 3 - \nThis double bedroom has a built in wardrobe/storage area which is shelved, laminate flooring in underfoot\n\nBedroom 4 - \nanother double bedroom with built in storage\n\nBedroom 5 - \nHaving laminate flooring and timber beams\n\nOutdoors - \nTimber entrance gates, gravel driveway and parking areaTimber side gatesPart brick facadeMature tree lined boundaries to side and rearWalled in front gardensDeck areaPaved cobble lock patio areaGarden shed\n\nIncluded in Sael - \nCarpets, window dressings, light fixtures & fittings, oven, hob, and garden shed\n\nResidents Association - \nVoluntary Contribution of 250.00 per annum\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Very sought after, exclusive address</li><li>Private mature tree lined site</li><li>Walking distance village centre, bus stops, local theatre,</li><li>Supermarkets etc</li><li>Adjacent Ratoath GAA grounds</li><li>Short walk to Ratoath playground</li><li>Short drive to Fairyhouse Racecourse, Tattersalls Country House and Bloodstock Sales, Emerald Park Theme Park</li><li>Easy access all major road networks - M2, M3, M50 Interchange and the Park & Ride facility at Dunboyne/Clonee</li><li>Blanchardstown Shopping Centre and Retail Park and Ashbourne shopping centre are a short drive</li><li>Beautiful features - Country style kitchen, latch doors, feature beams and ceilings.</li><li>Park brick facade front and rear</li><li>Feature brick fireplace and hearth in sitting room</li><li>Generous balance of reception rooms and bedrooms</li><li>Excellent flow to main reception rooms, linking to the garden</li><li>Very private gardens, not overlooked front or rear </li><li>No management fees - voluntary contribution to residents association of 250.00 annually approx.</li><li>Mains services, Mains sewerage, OFCH, Water filtration system, outdoor tap</ul>"
      },
